                    insight_sharptunnel:    `Sharp-tunnel trap: you read a smart-skill stall as a technical gap and threw more analysis at it. The model crept from 0.84 to 0.86 while the translation gap stayed wide open — so the steering committee rejected the readout a third time, for the same reason, and Bumi terminated. The model was never the problem.`,
                    insight_datadump:       `Data-dump rejected: the readout led with model performance instead of decisions — the very failure that got the first two readouts rejected. The board doesn't buy AUC; they buy decisions. Closing the translation gap was a smart-skill task, and it was skipped to the end.`,
                    insight_mixed:          `A partial recovery: some of the diagnosis landed, but the moves didn't fully reinforce each other — enough seams that the readout was a near miss rather than a clear win, and the flagship's renewal is still in doubt.`,
                    insight_ownerless:      `Ownerless client relationship: with “the whole pod” managing Bumi, no one was accountable, so the sponsor's requirements kept drifting unchallenged. Diffuse ownership reads to the client as no ownership — a single named owner was the cheapest unlock available, and it was left on the table.`,
                    insight_conflict:       `Conflict left unsurfaced: hoping the interpersonal and requirements tension would resolve itself let the scope keep drifting and cohesion stay low. Surfacing disagreement productively is a core smart skill — avoiding it isn't neutral, it's how the stall set in.`,
